         <div type="bio">
            <p>Actor and the second wife of composer <name type="person" key="hugh82">Herbert Hughes</name>. The daughter of Dublin shoemaker <name type="person" key="ID_MISSING">James</name> and <name type="person" key="ID_MISSING">Maria McKernan</name>, Susan McKernan lived in Drumcondra near the Joyces. As a young woman she moved to London. She attended the Academy of Dramatic Art and, in 1921, joined the Abbey Theatre breakaway company, The Irish Players, for the American tour of <name type="person" key="robi86">Lennox Robinson</name>’s <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">The White-Headed Boy</name>. She married Hughes in New Jersey the following year. After Herbert’s death in 1937 Suzanne remained in London, dying in Chelsea in December 1972. <hi rend="bold">John Simpson</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
